contentText:
Hit-Boy revealed that he and Nas have had a falling-out, despite the critically acclaimed work they&#8217;ve done together over the past several years.

The West Coast beatmaker sat down with DJ Vlad and Elliott Wilson recently and mentioned that he and the Queens legend aren&#8217;t on speaking terms anymore and he doesn&#8217;t see them ever collaborating again. &#8220;I ain&#8217;t spoke to Nas in three years,&#8221; Hit-Boy admitted. &#8220;We did six albums, 80 songs in three years. I produced almost every single song on his album that won a Grammy, King&#8217;s Disease .&#8221;

