He added: &#8220;We did a lot of great work, but I don&#8217;t see us working again.&#8221;

He was then asked by Wilson if there was any specific reason as to why they fell out, but Hit didn&#8217;t really want to get into specifics. &#8220;It&#8217;s a lot of reasons, you know what I mean?&#8221; he said. &#8220;But it&#8217;s something I don&#8217;t really wanna dig too deep in &#8217;cause the sh&#8211; is pretty deep. Respect to what we did get accomplished in three years.&#8221;

From 2020 to 2023, Nas and Hit-Boy made King&#8217;s Disease , King&#8217;s Disease II , Magic , King&#8217;s Disease III , Magic 2 and Magic 3 , with their King&#8217;s Disease series earning them three Grammy nominations, including a win for best rap album in 2021.

Billboard has reached out to Nas&#8217; team for comment.
